                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tenside",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00d36853-846c-3711-bbe3-faa2bf3fc5d3",
                                        "entry_id": "504f2c56-5922-3265-ab1d-cb1513e096f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surfactant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b7b9a0b-fd28-4935-a274-e879d94f7101",
                                                "sense_id": "00d36853-846c-3711-bbe3-faa2bf3fc5d3",
                                                "text": "Another large group of organic substances polluting the hydrosphere are the preparations known as tensides and detergents [115, 116]. Tensides are surface active substances with a capability to reduce the surface tension at an interface."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b35fc421-0fc0-479a-9bd6-d2da1b6b74ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "8c6e93cc-4bca-30e7-a2c5-595cf30a3671",
                        "source_sense_id": "b31c1b93-ac04-3eb2-b250-5d7f3a8f8efd",
                        "target_lang_word": "surfactant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "surfactant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94cf5191-5ba8-3422-9ce8-91f0981f282c",
                                        "entry_id": "6c38e680-66f4-3dfe-9dc2-8621c2ad28e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surface-active agent, or wetting agent, capable of reducing the surface tension of a liquid; typically organic compounds having a hydrophilic “head” and a hydrophobic “tail”."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6eaef187-dcc8-4ffc-a018-96fb605e28a5",
                                                "sense_id": "94cf5191-5ba8-3422-9ce8-91f0981f282c",
                                                "text": "Dr. Khorana added that this is especially true of cleansers that feature surfactants like sodium lauryl sulfate, as this class of ingredients can cause “dryness, irritation and eczema.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7bccd9a-099e-3cd5-8d2e-7dd62d0cf903",
                                        "entry_id": "6c38e680-66f4-3dfe-9dc2-8621c2ad28e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lipoprotein in the tissues of the lung that reduces surface tension and permits more efficient gas transport."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cad077e9-e337-4445-abec-8fa52eacea7a",
                                                "sense_id": "e7bccd9a-099e-3cd5-8d2e-7dd62d0cf903",
                                                "text": "It is conceivable that impairment of surfactant proteins is due to rheological and immunodefensive disorders of testis and epididymis or prostate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce499b40-e2f0-49b0-988e-fd0dc5269444",
                        "source_entry_id": "8c6e93cc-4bca-30e7-a2c5-595cf30a3671",
                        "source_sense_id": "b31c1b93-ac04-3eb2-b250-5d7f3a8f8efd",
                        "target_lang_word": "tensioactif",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
